          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score 500 points by winning tricks containing point cards and declaring melds.',
          gameplay: '1. Must follow suit. If unable, must trump if possible.\n2. **Bella**: Playing the King and Queen of trumps scores 20 points (must be announced).\n3. **Meld**: Sequences of 3 (20 pts) or 4 (50 pts) in the same suit score. Only the highest meld on either side scores for the team.\n4. **Last Trick**: 10 points.',
          keyRules: [
            'Trump ranking: Jack (20), Nine (14), Ace (11), Ten (10), King (4), Queen (3), Eight (0), Seven (0)',
            'Plain suit ranking: Ace (11), Ten (10), King (4), Queen (3), Jack (2), Nine (0), Eight (0), Seven (0)',
            'Must follow suit, must trump if cannot follow',
            'Bella bonus for King-Queen of trumps',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "If you hold the Jass (Jack) of trumps, you should almost always 'Take' the bid. 20 points is a massive head start in a 100+ point round.",
          intermediate: "The 'Ten' Lead: In plain suits, the 10 is very vulnerable to being captured by an Ace. Only lead a 10 if you have several of that suit or want to draw out the Ace early.",
          advanced: "Bidding with the Nell: If you hold the Nine of trumps and several other high plain cards, you can bid even without the Jack, provided you can force the Jack to be played on a trick you don't care about.",
          tips: [
            "Always announce 'Bella' when playing your King or Queen of trumps! Forgetting the call loses the 20-point bonus.",
            "The 7 of Trumps (The 'Seven of Diamonds' in many traditions) can be swapped for the face-up card if it was the trump-setter.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
